Z||000000||ArchMagi||03-06-2001||08:56 PM||||I was just thinking about rebuilding the 4cyl engine and i was wondering what tools were needs and the such.  Has anyone else done this? any info would be greatly appericeated.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-07-2001||09:24 PM||||I havent done one myself, but I can say probably a lot of tools!  Complete mechanics tool set; sockets/wrenches/screwdrivers/hand tools.  An engine stand to hold the block while you work on it.  Feeler gauges for gapping piston rings.  Cylender hone, valve spring compressor, a myraid of others probably.<P>I know I missed a bunch, but it's a start!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||03-07-2001||11:28 PM||||Torque Wrench! Tighten everything to recommended torque. I have learned the hard way (pistons through head on a Ford 60* V6) that guessing just ain't gonna cut it. Take your time, and make drawings or take pictures of how everything goes together. Good luck, and have fun!<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)||||reg||1
